Aim: Simulate systems and network logs to simulate incident reconstruction

Theory: Incident reconstruction in a core process in digital forensics where investigators analyze system and network logs logs to rebuild the sequence of events that occurred during a cyber attack.

The main goal is to identify

What happened

where it happened

How it happened

Who was involved

Log Correlation

Data is distributed across multiple systems

Log correlation combines these data sets to identify potterns and detect relationships.

Timeline Creation

Timaline is an open-source platform designed for log aggregates, and investigation.

Role of data

Dorker is used to simplify deployment and timesketch.

Timesketch has no multiple components. Web interface, database, search engine

Dorker ensures all of these components work together
